        "description": "<p><a href=\"https://www.gamespot.com/reviews/clair-obscur-expedition-33-review-light-and-shadow/1900-6418358/\">One Clair Obscur: Expedition 33</a> performer felt confident enough that the RPG would be a success that they bet someone at the game's publisher 33 baguettes that it would sell 1 million copies in a week. That ended up happening, and now the voice actor, Aliona Baranova, wants her bread.</p><p>At <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tHaRLkTkcxk\">Emerald City Comic Con 2026</a>, Baranova said she \"knew\" that Expedition 33 would be a hit. She raised the stakes, too, with a bread bet.</p><p>\"I made a bet with someone called Jack who's on the Kepler [Interactive] publishing team that it would sell a million copies in the first week. I made a bet and the bet was to win 33 baguettes. Jack, where are my baguettes?\" she said, <a href=\"https://www.gamesradar.com/games/rpg/baldurs-gate-3-performance-director-knew-clair-obscur-expedition-33-would-be-a-hit-and-even-took-a-bet-to-win",
